tion-Pathwidth-Outerplanar-Graphs-TR-UU-CS-2000-23.pdf` (Utrecht repository, hdl:1874/18990). pw(T*) ≤ pw(G) ≤ 2pw(T*) + 2.\n375:Still to obtain, mostly Elsevier open archive behind a browser check, none circumvented (full list with DOIs in the survey, §3): Skodinis 2003 (doi:10.1016/S0196-6774(02)00225-0); Scheffler 1990 (doi:10.1007/978-3-642-46908-4_70); Peng et al. 2000 (doi:10.1016/S0304-3975(99)00241-8); Chou, Ko, Ho & Chen 2008, block graphs (doi:10.1016/j.dam.2007.08.007); Ellis & Markov 2004 (doi:10.1016/j.ic.2004.03.005); Fomin & Thilikos 2006, Halin (doi:10.1016/j.jda.2005.06.004); Gustedt 1993 (doi:10.1016/0166-218X(93)90012-D); Takahashi, Ueno & Kajitani 1994 (doi:10.1016/0012-365X(94)90092-2); Megiddo et al. 1988 (doi:10.1145/42267.42268); Kneis et al. 2009 (doi:10.1137/080715482); Biedl 2022 (doi:10.1016/j.ipl.2021.106230); Coudert, Huc & Mazauric 2012 (doi:10.1007/s00453-011-9524-3); Yanasse 1996, *Pesquisa Operacional* 16(1), 1–26 (no DOI found).\n399:- Gustedt (1993), On the pathwidth of chordal graphs, *DAM* 45:233–248 — `1993-Gustedt-Pathwidth-Chordal-Graphs-DAM.pdf`\n412:- Bezrukov, Elsässer, Monien, Preis & Tillich (2004), New spectral lower bounds on the bisection width of graphs, *TCS* 320:155–174 — `2004-Bezrukov-...-TCS.pdf`\n418:- Kloks & Bodlaender (1992), Only few graphs have bounded treewidth, Utrecht tech report — `1992-Kloks-Bodlaender-Only-Few-Graphs-Bounded-Treewidth-TR-UU.pdf`\n43:# item 09 scratch witnesses (regenerable)\n54:# item 11 (loop0004): the bound harness adversary's scratch witnesses, regenerable\n59:reports/scratch/**/lit/\n60:reports/scratch/**/code_snapshot/\n61:reports/scratch/minor_certificates/vsanneal\n62:reports/scratch/mycielski_rec/anneal\n68:reports/scratch/obstruction_search/**/*.drat.gz\n72:reports/scratch/obstruction_search/13_pass1/certificates_1b/\n74:# loop0014 item 01: pdftotext extracts of held PDFs and of the untrusted ETH paper, regenerable (reports/scratch/subexp_pathwidth/01_audit/README.md)\n75:re