{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CgiTfsqzxMcacWupqGnXT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**3.4.1 (≤): sound.** Cuts inside `A` give `s ≤ n − 1`; after `A` plus `t` b's the count is `t + |N[S_{>t}]| = n + vs_σ(t)`; `t = 0` and `t = n` are covered (counts `n` and `0`). `n = 1` (`H = K₂`, `vs = 1 = 0 + 1`) fine.\n\n**3.4.1 (≥): sound in substance, one wording gap at `t = j`.** `j < n` is justified (A finishes first, so B's last vertex sits after `p`, hence at most `n − 1` b's precede it); the A/B swap is an automorphism; the \"cut just before `p`\" is the empty cut when `p = 1` and the inequality `k ≥ n − 1 + j` then reads `k ≥ 0`, harmless. The gap: the text says \"at the cut after the `t`-th b for `t ≥ j` (so after `p`)\", but for `t = j` the cut immediately after the `j`-th b lies *before* `p` (`A` incomplete there), and the \"cut just before `p`\" gives only `n − 1 + j`, which does not yield `n + vs_τ(j)` when `vs_τ(j) = j`. The needed cut is the one immediately *after* position `p`: all `n` a's and exactly `j` b's placed, count `j + (n − j) + vs_τ(j) = n + vs_τ(j)`. One clause fixes it (\"the cut after `p` at which `t` b's are placed\"). For `t = n` the claimed `k ≥ n + 0` follows from `t = n − 1 ≥ j`. `t < j` case correct.\n\n**3.4.2 (≤): sound.** Inside block `v = σ(t)` the counted copies of earlier vertices are exactly those of `u ∈ S_{<t}` with a neighbour in `S_{≥t}`, i.e. `c · vs_σ(t−1)`; the `i ≤ c − 1` placed copies of `v` count because their unplaced copies are neighbours. Block boundaries give `c · vs_σ(t)`.\n\n**3.4.2 (≥): sound.** At the cut before the last copy of `v_t`, every `u = v_s`, `s < t`, has all `c` copies placed (positions distinct), each adjacent to the unplaced last copy of its neighbour `w ⪰ v_t`; the `c − 1` other copies of `v_t` are disjoint from these; the set is `vs_τ(t − 1)` for `t − 1 = 1..n − 1`; `t − 1 = 0, n` are trivial. `n = 1` stated.\n\n**3.4.3 (cw ≤ vs(G°)): sound.** At the `G°`-cut just after the last port of `v_i`, all ports of `v_1..v_i` are placed; for a crossing edge `uw` either `(u,uw)` is counted (its edge-mate unplaced) or `(w,uw)` is placed and has an unplaced clique-mate (w's last port is after the cut, and it cannot be `(w,uw)` itself). Ports are per (vertex, edge), so charged ports are distinct per edge. Only blemish: \"last port\" is undefined for isolated vertices (they have none in `G°`); they contribute nothing to either side, so put them anywhere.\n\n**3.4.3 (vs(G°) ≤ cw + excess): sound.** Case check of `max(c + a, c + a + j (j < b), c + b)` over `a, b ∈ {0, 1, ≥2}` gives exactly `c + max(a,b) + max(0, min(a,b) − 1)`; `c + max(a,b) ≤ k` from the two gap cuts beside `v`; `min(a,b) ≤ ⌊(a+b)/2⌋ ≤ ⌊Δ/2⌋`; inter-clique cuts equal `G`-cuts ≤ `k`.\n\nBrute force (atlas to 6 vertices, `vs_subset_dp` / `cutwidth_dp`): 52 doubles, 18 graphs × `c ∈ {2,3}`, 126 expansions, zero violations; max excess by `Δ`: 0,0,0,0 at `Δ ≤ 3`, 1 at `Δ = 4, 5`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":664,"cache_read_input_tokens":72751,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":664,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01QGcCarNP8oabPFQf6S1XRB","agent_id":"a5ce94722e85af9b6","session_id":"8d527e6a-db35-43d6-976e-698f424f9f86","uuid":"95b9ae3a-cc7e-457c-a967-eb2115fbcae9","timestamp":"2026-11-04T19:44:16.920Z","request_id":"req_011CgiTfsWQtH8DcGd7jkzzc","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Refute the three §3.4 proofs"}
